module gunbc.observation_emit_census

import std.types { String, NonEmptyStr, Bool, List }
import std.dissolution { DissolutionCondition, unbound_dissolution, dissolution_description }
import std.nat { Nat }
import std.disposition { Disposition, Terminal, Scaffold, SingleAuthority }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }

data observation_emit_census_note: String = "P3 of the progress-and-observation lane: the census wall. Every place the floor emits a progress line today is either a PROJECTION of the observation event stream (migrated, P1/P2) or a COUNTED FRONTIER ROW carrying a reason and a dissolve-on — the same discipline the site subsumption lane uses for unthemed colours. This module is the census authority: the classification is a closed sum, so a site cannot be half-classified, and the roster below names the structured-tag emit families that exist in the seed today. The executable hygiene witness is bidirectional: it reds when a rostered marker vanishes AND when a known live tag family is missing from the roster, so growth after the snapshot cannot silently understate."

data observation_emit_census_sequencing_note: String = "Sequencing, per the operator ruling and live-log review (run 30142403230): tagged migrations landed (gantt, governor, typecheck-attribution, measurement, shell with named-intent subjects; Ambient ShellTrace Suppressed at Normal). Post-census growth tags ([floor-drain], [receipt], [file], and #7205's [resolve-split]/[assembly-split]) are CountedFrontierSite rows so the roster cannot silently understate. [gate-warm-cost] and [witness-row-cost-drift] were rows here until 2026-08-11, and #7284's [witness-row-cost-migration-disclosure] until 2026-08-22, each leaving when its raw emit was deleted outright rather than migrated. [floor-memory] LEFT THE ROSTER ON 2026-08-26 AND IT IS NOT ONE OF THESE DEPARTURES, WHICH IS THE FINDING. The marker and its render_heartbeat_line_mirror are gone from the seed (measured: no occurrence of either anywhere under src/, only one doc comment naming the mirror), and read no further that looks exactly like the three retirements above -- an emit deleted at the root, a row simply absent. It is the opposite. The floor still emits a periodic progress line and a per-claim RSS growth line; they are now [floor-heartbeat] and [floor-claim-memory], raw formatted eprintlns in cli_run.rs with no projection behind them. So a MIGRATED row's projection was DELETED and raw emits took over its job under new names -- a reversal, not a retirement. Both successors are on the roster above as CountedFrontierSite, which moves the frontier count UP by two. THE NEAR-MISS IS WHY THIS IS WRITTEN AT LENGTH: the row was first deleted as a completed retirement on the evidence that its marker was gone, and marker-absence is exactly as consistent with a reversal as with a retirement. The census cannot tell them apart by looking at the row that vanished; only by asking what now does the job. That question is not asked by any check here, and it is a second face of the same missing discovery the completeness note names -- an unrostered successor is invisible for precisely the reason an unrostered new family is. THIS NOTE PREVIOUSLY GROUNDED [witness-row-cost] ON `claim_executor discovery_claim_result`, AND THAT FUNCTION DOES NOT EXIST -- not renamed, not moved: no declaration by that name is anywhere in the seed, and the surviving [witness-row-cost] refusals are the witness_cost_* helpers in cli_run.rs. The citation was fabricated at the moment it was written, in the same 2026-08-22 change that restored the row on a correct premise, and it was copied from here into test.claim.observation_raw_print_retirement_acceptance_test, so one invented symbol became two files' evidence. The family is still live and still on the roster; only the symbol naming its occurrence was false."

type EmitSiteDisposition
  = MigratedToObservation { via: NonEmptyStr }
  | CountedFrontierSite { reason: NonEmptyStr, dissolution: DissolutionCondition }

data emit_site_disposition_note: String = "A closed sum, so a site is exactly one of two things and never silently neither. MigratedToObservation names the projection that replaced the raw emit — the evidence the site now speaks the event vocabulary. CountedFrontierSite carries a reason it has not migrated yet and the trigger that will dissolve it, so the debt is countable and prioritizable rather than an open-ended intention. There is no third arm, which is the point: an emit site the census has not looked at cannot be represented here, so the roster's completeness is what the witness checks against the seed."

type CensusedEmitSite {
  marker: NonEmptyStr
  disposition: EmitSiteDisposition
}

data censused_emit_site_has_no_source_file_note: String = "A ROW NAMES A TAG FAMILY, NOT A FILE, AND THE FIELD THAT NAMED A FILE IS DELETED (2026-08-26). CensusedEmitSite carried source_file: NonEmptyStr, whose sole consumer anywhere in the corpus was the witness's census_marker_present, which read that one file and grepped it. That is a positional citation in the sense §3 rules against -- a second naming scheme for something the seed already contains -- and it rots in the one way this census cannot tolerate: it goes false when the emit MOVES, which is not a census fact at all. It did. #9228 deleted claim_executor's unreachable plan/walk surface (21,366 -> 11,508 lines) and the file-pinned rows went red five at once -- floor-memory, receipt, resolve-split, assembly-split, witness-row-cost -- of which exactly ONE was a real census event (floor-memory's emit left the seed, and its row is deleted accordingly) and four were the pin rotting while the tag family sat untouched in a sibling seed file. A check whose red says `the code moved` where the census asks `does this still emit` is measuring the wrong quantity, and four false reds beside one true one is worse than no check, because the true one is indistinguishable in the noise. What replaces it is seed_emit_sources below: presence is searched across the SEED, so a marker that moves between seed files stays green and a marker that leaves the seed reds. The denominator became the thing the census is actually about."

data seed_emit_sources: List<String> = [
  "src/v1/stage0/src/bin/claim_executor.rs",
  "src/v1/stage0/src/bin/claim_batch.rs",
  "src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run.rs",
  "src/v1/stage0/src/v1_interpreter.rs",
  "src/v1/stage0/src/v1_rt.rs",
  "src/v1/stage0/src/memory_governor.rs"
]

data seed_emit_sources_note: String = "THE CENSUS'S DENOMINATOR: the seed files a tagged progress emit can live in. Presence of a rostered marker is asked of this SET, never of one named file, which is what makes a row survive #9228-shaped code movement and red only when the tag family actually leaves the seed. THIS LIST IS ITSELF HAND-MAINTAINED AND THAT IS THE RESIDUE, stated rather than hidden: a seed file dropped from it narrows the search silently, which is the empty-observation narrow this repository names as strictly worse than a widen. It is mitigated, not closed -- the witness asserts every listed source reads non-empty, so a path that stops existing reds instead of quietly contributing nothing, and the list is one authority for the whole census rather than a pin per row, so it cannot rot thirteen different ways. What would close it is the source-derived denominator both this module's witness and the retirement acceptance already name as their residue: the seed's tagged emits DISCOVERED at occurrence grain from syntax, joined against this roster, reporting live-but-unrostered and rostered-but-absent simultaneously. That discovery is unbuilt, and until it lands this list is the honest approximation of it."

data floor_heartbeat_site: CensusedEmitSite = CensusedEmitSite {
  marker: "[floor-heartbeat]" as NonEmptyStr,
  disposition: CountedFrontierSite {
    reason: "THE SUCCESSOR TO THE RETIRED [floor-memory] MIGRATION, AND ITS ARRIVAL IS A REGRESSION RATHER THAN GROWTH. floor-memory was a MigratedToObservation row: the floor's periodic progress line was a projection of the observation event stream through gunbc.observation_ci_render.ci_heartbeat_line, rendered by the seed mirror render_heartbeat_line_mirror. Measured 2026-08-26, that mirror does not occur anywhere under src/ -- only one doc comment names it -- and the periodic line the floor actually emits is this raw formatted eprintln. So the projection was deleted and a raw emit took the same job under a new tag. The row is CountedFrontierSite because that is what the site now IS, not because it was newly discovered: a census that recorded the disappearance of floor-memory as a completed retirement, with no row for what replaced it, would have booked a reversal as progress" as NonEmptyStr,
    dissolution: unbound_dissolution(description: "restore the heartbeat projection: the periodic floor line is rendered by gunbc.observation_ci_render.ci_heartbeat_line again (the .dag projection still exists and is still witnessed by test.claim.observation_ci_render_witness_test -- what is missing is the seed calling it), at which point this row becomes MigratedToObservation and [floor-claim-memory] follows it")
  }
}

data floor_claim_memory_site: CensusedEmitSite = CensusedEmitSite {
  marker: "[floor-claim-memory]" as NonEmptyStr,
  disposition: CountedFrontierSite {
    reason: "the per-claim and worst-claim RSS growth lines emitted beside the heartbeat above, raw and formatted in the seed with no observation projection behind them. Same family and same regression as [floor-heartbeat]: this is the memory half of what [floor-memory] used to carry as a MeasurementSegment projection" as NonEmptyStr,
    dissolution: unbound_dissolution(description: "the same restoration as [floor-heartbeat] -- a MeasurementSegment projection carries the RSS growth, rather than a formatted string")
  }
}

